## Source-bounded blockers

1. `assign_open_front_boundary_authority()` requires an entry from `edge_matching_indices()` before classifying a boundary edge. That index intentionally contains only two-face interior edges, so a genuine one-face source boundary is rejected by construction.
2. Materialization counts an internal isolation seam as consumed only when it appears in cell-boundary `transitionSourceEdges`, then requires every retained region seam. Review must decide a complete exact consumption witness; unconditional marking or count/order/ID/proximity inference is forbidden.
3. The two semantic-digest counterfactual tests live only in `tests/MilestoneGP27Tests.cpp`, which belongs to the disabled historical target. They are absent from the immutable package.
4. Several mandated quotient and retention counterfactuals have no independently discoverable default packaged test; retention has positive `true` evidence but no `false` counterpart.

## Process decision

The optional review policy remains `never`, but the mandatory process guard overrides it. Retained direct authority regressed and the quotient consumed no region/seam/relation authority after the review-approved Code + Build. **No ordinary Code + Build is authorized until Review approves, amends, or replaces the proposed remediation architecture.**

The proposed implementation scope in the runtime report is `proposed_pending_review`. It may not be executed directly.

## Turn boundary

The next Review may inspect source, tests, build wiring, reports, and immutable evidence read-only. It may not edit production/tests/build files, configure, compile, run tests/benchmarks, or regenerate discovery.

Every completed turn ends with a new top-level PR #8 conversation comment after all other repository writes. PR #8 remains open, draft, unmerged.
